# Chat Module Parity

Every chat module in the app shares the same code and must look and behave
identically. `pages/wiseai.html` is the reference chat module. When you touch
any chat surface, all others must still match.

## Required in every chat module

- **Three-dot menu** with the ability to open/view the sticky history module,
  plus the standard options. Sticky modules are the only mode — do not add a
  toggle to switch sticky on/off. History starts **collapsed** to the icon
  rail on every load; the history icon expands it in-session, and
  history off collapses it.
- **"What can I ask?"** panel that opens inside the chat window and can break
  out. Its headline uses the brand **serif** font. It must actually open (not
  just render content behind the scenes).
- **Intent chips** that are clickable, actionable, and each open a real
  transcript. The chip icon is **brand blue** (gold only on “What can I ask?”),
  and the right-side text label animates like the reference. Intent chips
  **never have a tooltip** — no hover card, no native `title`, no `data-tip`.
  The label on the chip is the whole story.
- **Every transcript ends on topic chips.** Regardless of which chat or
  which answer just landed, the thread must close with intent chips related
  to that transcript and topic — never a dead-end reply. Prefer the chip's
  own `nextIntents` (or the host's `followups` map); otherwise pick leftover
  unused chips from the current topic set, or score the surface's catalog
  against the live thread. Hosts may still `setIntents()` to swap a curated
  follow-up row. Mid-turn status cards (`trailChips: false`) are the only
  exception — chips trail the actual answer, not the card.
- **Streaming** paragraph-by-paragraph output (then the thumbs row, then
  intent chips). Do not regress to word-by-word typing or the old pulsating
  three-dot loader as the primary style.
- **Helix animation** matches `pages/wiseai.html` — the published **Scene**
  pose in `BGANIM_PUBLISH_POSE` (see the helix-settings-from-wiseai rule).
  Close-up stays available as a Load chip. Never invent a per-page pose.
- **Unlocked composer** — no lock icon, no readonly input. Typing is live.
  Sending any distinctive word from an intent chip (label, ask, or intent id)
  plays that chip's transcript, the same as clicking the chip.
- **Default width** is single on viewports ≤ 1512 CSS px and double when wider
  (see the chat-module-width rule). Do not force single on load.
- Anything that happens in a related right-hand module (e.g. the Nutrition
  Facts panel on `add-product.html`) must be reflected in the chat as if the
  assistant did it.

## Rules for the agent

- After editing one chat module, verify the others still satisfy this list.
- Never let a chat module drift into a bespoke variant — fix it to match
  wiseai.html.
